{"id":"fd82d9dd0321dac0f15efe1474be4e923ecef750","axis":"silent","repo":"payloadcms/payload","sha":"fd82d9dd0321dac0f15efe1474be4e923ecef750","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","lines":["@@ -385,6 +385,13 @@ const docs = await payload.find({"," "," ### Writing CSS"," ","+**Support document and Shadow DOM contexts when writing or reviewing shared CSS:**","+","+- Define shared token defaults on both `:root` and `:host`, including defaults inside media queries.","+- Include equivalent shadow-host selectors for theme and enhanced-contrast rules, e.g. `html[data-enhanced-contrast] .control` and `:host([data-enhanced-contrast]) .control`. Apply this to component-specific adjustments as well as shared palettes.","+- Preserve existing document selector specificity. Adding `:host` to a parent selector list can raise the specificity of nested rules. Flatten those nested rules when necessary to preserve application overrides.","+- Keep document-only resets and Admin Panel layout styles scoped to the document. For shared token or theme changes, verify the affected states in both contexts, loading the stylesheet inside the shadow root for that case.","+"," Stylelint enforces the rules below on `.css` files (SCSS is no longer linted and is being phased out). Run `pnpm run lint:css` to check, or `pnpm run lint` to run all linters."," "," **Mobile-first media queries only - never `max-width`:**"],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/admin/customizing-css.mdx","lines":["@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ Here is an example of how you might target the Dashboard View and change the bac"," "," ### Specificity rules"," ","-All Payload CSS is encapsulated inside CSS layers under `@layer payload-default`. Any custom css will now have the highest possible specificity.","+Payload's default styles and design tokens are declared in `@layer payload-default`. Unlayered custom CSS takes precedence over these normal declarations, regardless of selector specificity or stylesheet load order."," "," We have also provided a layer `@layer payload` if you want to use layers and ensure that your styles are applied after payload."," ","@@ -45,13 +45,13 @@ To override existing styles in a way that the previous rules of specificity woul"," "," ```css"," @layer payload-default {","-  // my styles within the Payload specificity","+  /* my styles within the Payload specificity */"," }"," ```"," "," ## Re-using Payload CSS variables"," ","-Payload exposes its design tokens as global [CSS Variables](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Using_CSS_custom_properties). These are defined globally on `:root`, so you can consume them in your own stylesheets without importing anything.","+Payload defines its design tokens as [CSS Variables](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Using_CSS_custom_properties) on both `:root` and `:host`. Custom admin components inherit these tokens without importing anything."," "," ```css"," @layer payload-default {","@@ -62,6 +62,30 @@ Payload exposes its design tokens as global [CSS Variables](https://developer.mo"," }"," ```"," ","+### Overriding tokens","+","+Override token values on `:root` in your own unlayered CSS:","+","+```css","+:root {","+  --button-radius: 19px;","+}","+```","+","+<Banner type=\"info\">Inside Shadow DOM, override tokens on `:host`.</Banner>","+","+### Using tokens outside the Admin Panel","+","+Import `@payloadcms/ui/css/tokens` to use Payload's design tokens outside the Admin Panel without loading its resets, component styles, fonts, or global element styles:","+","+```ts","+import '@payloadcms/ui/css/tokens'","+```","+","+For Shadow DOM, load the stylesheet into the shadow root itself. A normal CSS import may place it in the outer document instead.","+","+Values in `rem` use the document's root font size, including inside Shadow DOM. Load the fonts you want and apply typography tokens in your own styles.","+"," ## CSS Library"," "," To make it as easy as possible for you to override default styles, Payload uses [BEM naming conventions](http://getbem.com/) for all CSS within the Admin UI. If you provide your own CSS, you can override any built-in styles easily, including targeting nested components and their various component states.","@@ -74,11 +98,11 @@ The following variables are defined and can be overridden:"," - [Colors](https://github.com/payloadcms/payload/blob/main/packages/ui/src/css/colors.css)","   - Semantic tokens for background, text, border, and icon colors (e.g. `--color-bg`, `--color-text`, `--color-border`, `--color-icon`)","   - Success / warning / danger color tokens","-  - The raw `--ramp-*` color palette","+  - [The raw `--ramp-*` color palette](https://github.com/payloadcms/payload/blob/main/packages/ui/src/css/color-ramps.css)"," - [Sizing](https://github.com/payloadcms/payload/blob/main/packages/ui/src/css/app.css)","-  - Horizontal gutter","-  - Transition speeds","-  - Font sizes","+  - [Horizontal gutter](https://github.com/payloadcms/payload/blob/main/packages/ui/src/css/spacing.css)","+  - Navigation width","+  - [Font sizes](https://github.com/payloadcms/payload/blob/main/packages/ui/src/css/typography.css)","   - Etc."," "," For an up-to-date, comprehensive list of all available variables, please refer to the [Source Code](https://github.com/payloadcms/payload/blob/main/packages/ui/src/css).","@@ -90,4 +114,8 @@ For an up-to-date, comprehensive list of all available variables, please refer t"," "," #### Dark Mode"," ","-Colors are designed to automatically adapt to the theme of the [Admin Panel](./overview). All `--color-*` tokens are redefined under `[data-theme='dark']`, so semantic tokens like `--color-bg` and `--color-text`, along with the success / warning / danger colors, adjust automatically for dark mode.","+Colors are designed to automatically adapt to the theme of the [Admin Panel](./overview). Theme-dependent `--color-*` tokens are redefined under `[data-theme='dark']` and `:host([data-theme='dark'])`, so semantic tokens like `--color-bg` and `--color-text`, along with the success / warning / danger colors, adjust automatically for dark mode.","+","+Tokens default to light mode. Set `data-theme=\"dark\"` or `data-theme=\"light\"` on the document's `<html>` element or on the shadow host to select its palette. Add `data-enhanced-contrast` to that same element to enable enhanced contrast, including nested themed controls.","+","+A nested `data-theme` changes colors and elevations while inheriting shared spacing, typography, radii, and component customizations."],"additions":36,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/plugin-seo/src/fields/colors.css","lines":["@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@"," @layer payload-default {","   :root,","+  :host,","   [data-theme] {","     --seo-description-color: #9a9a9a;","     --seo-danger-bg: red;","@@ -13,7 +14,9 @@","   }"," ","   html[data-enhanced-contrast],","-  html[data-enhanced-contrast] [data-theme] {","+  html[data-enhanced-contrast] [data-theme],","+  :host([data-enhanced-contrast]),","+  :host([data-enhanced-contrast]) [data-theme] {","     --seo-description-color: var(--color-text-secondary);","     --seo-danger-bg: var(--color-bg-danger);","     --seo-short-bg: var(--color-bg-danger);"],"additions":4,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ui/bundle.js","lines":["@@ -83,25 +83,19 @@ async function build() {","   })"," ","   try {","-    // The esbuild pass above bundles only component styles. The design tokens","-    // live in `src/css/*.css` (referenced via `src/styles.css`'s `@import`","-    // chain). `copyfiles` also copies `src/styles.css` to `dist/styles.css`,","-    // but the write below would overwrite it — dropping the tokens entirely.","-    // Consumers that load `styles.css` directly (the `@payloadcms/ui/css`","-    // export, and `css/app.css`'s `@import '../styles.css'`) would then get","-    // components with no CSS custom properties, so every `var(--spacer-*)`","-    // resolves empty (e.g. switch toggles collapse to 0×0). Prepend the token","-    // chain so the published `styles.css` is a complete, self-contained sheet.","-    // Read the tokens straight from `src/css/*.css` so this works regardless of","-    // `directoryArg` (e.g. `dist` for the normal build, `esbuild` for the","-    // bundle-size analysis build, which `copyfiles` does not populate).","+    // Writing esbuild's component styles alone would overwrite the base stylesheet copied by copyfiles.","+    // Include the entry's imports and global rules so published styles retain the tokens that prevent controls from collapsing.","+    // Read from source because copyfiles does not populate alternative output directories such as esbuild.","     const stylesEntry = fs.readFileSync('src/styles.css', 'utf8')","-    const tokenCss = [...stylesEntry.matchAll(/@import\\s+['\"]\\.\\/(css\\/[^'\"]+)['\"]/g)]","-      .map((match) => fs.readFileSync(path.join('src', match[1]), 'utf8'))","-      .join('\\n')","+","+    const baseCss = stylesEntry.replace(","+      /@import\\s+['\"]\\.\\/(css\\/[^'\"]+)['\"];?/g,","+      (_import, relativePath) => fs.readFileSync(path.join('src', relativePath), 'utf8'),","+    )","+","     const componentCss = fs.readFileSync('dist-styles/index.css', 'utf8')"," ","-    fs.writeFileSync(`${directoryArg}/styles.css`, `${tokenCss}\\n${componentCss}`, 'utf8')","+    fs.writeFileSync(`${directoryArg}/styles.css`, `${baseCss}\\n${componentCss}`, 'utf8')","     fs.rmSync('dist-styles', { recursive: true })","   } catch (err) {","     console.error(`Error while bundling styles.css and removing dist-styles: ${err}`)"],"additions":10,"deletions":16,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/ui/package.json","lines":["@@ -322,6 +322,7 @@","       \"default\": \"./src/forms/fieldSchemasToFormState/renderField.tsx\"","     },","     \"./css/app.css\": \"./src/css/app.css\",","+    \"./css/tokens\": \"./src/css/tokens.css\",","     \"./assets\": {","       \"import\": \"./src/assets/index.ts